---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Metabolic Intelligence"
  description="About: Metabolic Intelligence — designed for Klere (klere.ai). Edge + resource-optimized central (not uncapped hyperscale). Water/power/cooling plants not required by design. board_synth_claimed=false."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Paper 4 · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Metabolic Intelligence
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      A new form of AI <strong class="text-brand-white">designed for Klere</strong> (<a href="https://klere.ai" class="text-brand-cyan">klere.ai</a>) — academic thesis, economic argument, and market value proposition. Research owns the MEI class; Klere owns the product embodiment. Budget-native computer intelligence: a budget goes in; the best answer that budget can buy comes out.
      Designed for the <strong class="text-brand-white">edge</strong> and the <strong class="text-brand-white">resource-optimized central datacenter</strong> — not uncapped hyperscale.
      At those lower energy budgets, dedicated water, power, and hyperscale cooling plants are <strong class="text-brand-white">not required by design</strong>
      (design consequence of the budget-native class + pack evidence: µW tags; grid-following lean campus — not invented liters saved).
      Digital enzymes at microwatt cold-chain tags; OpenADR / DSX Flex lean-campus service at a budget-capped 100 MW plant.
      Class properties: physics-informed, test-time inference, zero-shot under grammar, sequential / super learning,
      no large pretrain required on the enzyme path. Runs on GPUs and MCUs today; points at neuromorphic,
      analog / in-memory, photonic, and reversible / adiabatic substrates. Soft-ref path:
      <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>; estimates ≠ package
      <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
      Status: research study, not a journal final. Figures under /living/mei/ are static pack companions (Manim later).
      Tag microwatts are datasheet + schedule model; MCU counts are emulator-measured; campus Wh are curves / ledger;
      protocols in the service are real; the plant is a model. Chicken-spoilage Anwar results are internal only, not published.
      Peer overlap is cited honestly: V-JEPA zero-shot conflicts with no-pretrain unless scoped to the enzyme path;
      Logical Intelligence constraint energy is not campus joules.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-laws">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion laws</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Catalog triad stays intact:
        <a href="/papers/mol/" class="text-brand-cyan">Navigation</a> (Mixture of Limits) ·
        <a href="/papers/ni/" class="text-brand-cyan">Commit</a> (Notational Intelligence) ·
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="text-brand-cyan">Economic Reality of Satiation</a>.
        Fourth study: <strong class="text-brand-white">Energy budget / Metabolic Intelligence</strong> (this study).
        See <a href="/#companion-laws" class="text-brand-cyan">catalog triad</a> and
        <a href="/#metabolic-intelligence" class="text-brand-cyan">energy-budget strip</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/mei/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/mei/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/mei.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/mei/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Interactive figures
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 glass-card p-6 space-y-3" id="klere-positioning">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Klere positioning (one page)</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">What Klere is.</strong> Product home for Metabolic Intelligence
        (<a href="https://klere.ai" class="text-brand-cyan">klere.ai</a>). Research owns the MEI class;
        Klere owns embodiment. Public site is thin access framing — not a shipped feature catalog.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Where it runs.</strong> <em>Edge</em> (coin-cell tags, enzyme recognition, metabolic schedule)
        and <em>resource-optimized central</em> (budget-capped, grid-following lean campus under OpenADR / DSX Flex).
        Not an uncapped transformer hyperscale campus.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Ecosystem claim (allowed).</strong> At these energy budgets, dedicated water plants,
        dedicated power plants, and hyperscale cooling loops are <strong class="text-brand-white">not required by design</strong>
        — design consequence of the envelope + pack evidence (µW tags; lean campus). 
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Forbidden without meters:</strong> invented liters/gallons saved, Wh/answer as board
        <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code>, AEMA latency numbers, Anwar chicken accuracy.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">GTM slices.</strong> (1) Edge pack — proven recognition/schedule evidence; roadmap SKU.
        (2) Lean-campus flexibility — proven protocol demos + scenario table; roadmap operator product.
        (3) Obtain/stack — proven router math / soft-ref companions; roadmap gateway packaging.
        Sell proven pack and roadmap as separate evidence classes. Soft-ref:
        <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Vs hyperscale transformers.</strong> Envelope-first, Model LAST, dual-scale actuators —
        not pretrain→unlimited import. Peers (Logical Intelligence, World Labs/V-JEPA, Dynamo/DSX/AEMA, neuromorphic MCUs)
        own slices; none presently combine tag↔lean-campus + OpenADR/DSX + J(m|q) + enzymes as one class.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 glass-card p-6 space-y-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Paths</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/papers/mei/</span> → study prose</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/pdfs/mei.pdf</span> → downloadable study PDF</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/living/mei/</span> → static teaching figures (pack charts)</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Measurement bounds</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Datasheet + schedule ≠ board package power. Emulator instruction counts ≠ wattmeter.
        Curves / ledger Wh are labeled estimates or measured-kernel models.
        Soft-ref path: <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code> only when Metered;
        <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
